# DTF tier manifest: oci-last-tag-delete-by-digest
#   artifact-keeper#1683 (1.12.0, third slice): manifest GET/HEAD/DELETE by
#   digest, the referrers API and the storage GC orphan predicate key on the
#   oci_manifests existence table instead of deriving existence from oci_tags.
#
# Profile-set: filesystem + gc.oci-manifests-reconcile-fast (the reconcile
# every 15 s). Images are pushed over /v2 with curl (config, one layer, a
# curl-built OCI manifest or index), as oci-manifests-reconcile does. Storage
# GC is run through POST /api/v1/admin/storage-gc. The filesystem volume is
# read with a throwaway postgres:16-alpine container (--volumes-from the
# backend; the backend image has no shell), as storage-integrity does.
#
# THE GATES (RED ak-backend:1.11.5, GREEN on the #1683 readers image)
#   (CONTROL) push app:v1, delete the only tag: GET and HEAD by digest answer
#             404 and the oci_manifests row is gone (#4449, 1.11.0).
#   (FIX)     a row the last-tag delete of a 1.11 replica could leave behind
#             (re-inserted with SQL and aged past the 600 s minimum) answers
#             404 by digest and the reconcile removes it within 75 s; RED on
#             1.11.5: the row stays (no reconcile).
#   (FIX)     an image pushed, a signature pushed by digest with the image as
#             its subject, then the image's only tag deleted:
#             GET .../referrers/<subject> lists nothing; the signature itself
#             still pulls by digest. RED on 1.11.5: the referrer is listed.
#   (FIX)     the child of a tagged index, pushed under its own tag that is
#             then deleted: GET child by digest is 200 and stays 200 after a
#             storage GC run, its object stays on disk. RED on 1.11.5: 404 by
#             digest (the trashed row of the image counts as deleted).
#   (FIX)     the child of an index whose tag then moved to another image (the
#             index is untagged but pulls by digest): a storage GC run keeps
#             the child's object, and both pull by digest. RED on 1.11.5: GC
#             deletes the child's object (it only protects children of TAGGED
#             indexes).
#
# Wall clock: about 2 min (75 s wait for the reconcile on 1.11.5).
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: not under test.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem gc.oci-manifests-reconcile-fast"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
